Quadris for Series 3

This is an adaptation of Quadris for the Psion LZ, (which was itself a
variation on a well-known theme). Despite reduced-size playing area, Quadris
presents a challenging game (without the eye strain you will get playing
other, less well-designed versions).

QUADRIS IS NOT FREE - IT IS SHAREWARE. That means, if you wish to use it,
you should pay the registration fee. It only costs œ5 (or $10 US) to register. This helps to pay for the many hours of work that went into writing Quadris. It is a small price to pay, and doing so encourages authors to continue to write high-quality software.

Please send your œ5, together with name and address details, to MG Andon,
25 Tunstall Road, London SW9 8BZ, England.
Please note that overseas users can send the equivalent in local currency
(cash is the most convenient method).

INSTALLING QUADRIS
Quadris must be installed as follows:
The file QUAD.APP can go in any directory on any drive (the usual place is
in the \app\ directory. You must put the file QUAD.PIC in a subdirectory of
the directory in which QUAD.APP resided. That subdirectory must be named
\quad\.
For example: if you put QUAD.APP in m:\app\, you must put QUAD.PIC in
m:\app\quad\. You can then install the icon in your system screen, in the
usual way.

PLAYING QUADRIS
Quadris plays from left to right (new tiles drop from the left, to build
walls on the right. Note that it is not a copy of Tetris. There are six
levels - variations include moving baseline and a partially-obscured playing
area. Tiles also drop faster as you progress.

The controls are simple. Use the vertical arrow keys to shift the current
tile up or down; use the horizontal arrows to rotate it. The Space bar
drops the tile rapidly.
One of the most important keys is Enter, which freezes the dropping tile
and releases a new tile. Using this key you can build high walls before
allowing them to collapse - you score far more points this way.
Other keys are Help (for help), P to pause the game, and Esc (to quit).
Note that the game also pauses if you switch off the Series 3, or move to
another application.

Enjoy Quadris - comments and suggestions welcome.

